{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Added `POST /v1/api-keys/{apiKeyID}/regenerate`. It replaces the key's token in place with a single UPDATE scoped to the authenticated user, so the old token stops authenticating immediately and the new one works; it returns the API key object with the new `token` (200). Unknown or other users' key IDs return 404, an invalid ID returns 400. `last_used_at` is reset to NULL on regeneration. Also added `RegenerateAPIKey` / `RegenerateAPIKeyContext` to the Go client. Existing build and tests pass; the new endpoint has no test of its own.", "t": 1794462035.112}
